.TH SMTSTAT 1
.SH NAME
smtstat \- what the dataset holds, in tables of text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smtstat
[
.B \-t
.I seconds
]
[
.I dataset.tsv
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I smtstat
reads a dataset as
.IR smtdata (1)
writes one, from the file named or from the standard input, and describes it,
a table after a line that says what it holds.
A tab separates one field from the next, so that
.IR awk (1)
may take any table apart.
.PP
The tables, in order: the dataset by count; the text columns and the values each takes;
the numeric columns with their least value, quartiles, median, greatest value, mean and
deviation, the time in seconds and in its base 10 logarithm;
the logarithm by bins a tenth wide, with the timeouts in each bin;
the outcomes by logic; the families, largest first;
and the Spearman correlation of every feature with the targets.
.PP
The regression target is the base 10 logarithm of the wall clock time, a timeout
counted at twice
.I seconds
.RB ( \-t ,
1200 by default).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
The description of a dataset:
.RS
.nf
smtstat dataset.tsv > stat.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
The ten features whose Spearman correlation with the time is the highest:
.RS
.nf
awk \-F\(rs\(rst \-v OFS=\(rs \(rs \(aa/^feature/{t=1; next} t && NF==4 {print $2, $1}\(aa stat.txt \e
	| sort \-k1,1gr | sed 10q
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IR smtdata (1),
.IR smtfit (1)
